        <p>BlLck to move and win.</p>
        <p>The above problem was one of the adjudicated endings in the Warringtan v. Cairo-street match on Monday last This ending 'occurred on No. 6 board between mecsrs. F Wright (Black) and W. Warbur- ton (White.)The two Captaino,Mr. F. Dunne and Mr. e. Tavlin, eban(loned the ending as a draw, but Mr. Torithinson, who was an onlooker, pointed out a win or the Cairo-street player. As various opinions 13reva1l, however, as to the soundnes of the win, Mr. T • oklnanson offers a prize of any book on the game to the value of 53 to any player vv-lo can t•diow ae 89and draw for White. All solutions to be r ceiv Vie he atthis office notlater than Friday morning. all give Mr. Tomkinson's next week.</p>
        <p>SOLVERS LIST. Previous Prob. Total</p>
        <p>score No 73. Pts. T, p For'oes.Warrington —.—.... ...... 114 2 116 E Ogden, Warrington Rickets, W,arrington _____.—...lo9 2 111 Rowe, Warrington 2 103 W Mavey, 99 2 101 IV Darlington, Penketti....._ ..... 99 2 101 J Evans, 99 2 101 J Foden, Warrington . .... 98 2 100 Ruttr, Warrington 91 2 93 "E JP" 89 2 91 J Green, 88 2 90 "C ,"Warrington A Banner, Warrington ..... .—.—.... 53 53 W Rigbv, Warrington .— 44 2 45 -W Hewitt, Warrington ..... .31 2 33 A Gabriel, Stockton Heath ............ 31 2 33 T Broornhall, Earlestown 3O 30 J. J. Wright, Warrington 18 18 WB. Kean. Warrington......_ _..... 18 18 HPowell, Warrington ._._.— ~.—... 11 2 13 E Donaghy, Warrington F Frangleton, Warrington —....—._ 4 4 T. Guuld, Warrington ..... ..—.--... 2 2 4</p>
        <p>We have to announce that the winner of our Coln- Petition for February is Mr. T P Forbes, 6, Church- Street Warrington.</p>
        <p>NOTlCE.—Solvers who become entitled to a prize lo this competition can, if they desire, have any book on the game of Draughts equal to the value of ss. instead of cash prize, by notifying the Draughts Editor.</p>
        <p>In connection with the above competition we ' offer a monthly prize of ss. to the competitor who zucceeds in placing himself at the head of the Solvers' List at the end of the month. Where the prize is awarded the winnPrs' score is cancelled, While the remainimg competitors' points go towards the next mouths competition. The winner may re- enter the tourney if he chooses, commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as 'follows : Two for the correct solution of a prob- lem ; two for correcting the author's terms, one for showing a dual solution or a dual key-move, and one for showing a dual continuation at any stage in the solution.</p>
