        <p>INFLUENZA. INCREASING.</p>
        <p>Thu Influenza Epidemic is again spreading over the Couutry. 'Thl visicatioa is of a very prostrating neture, and the disease is certainly on the increase. The origin of the disease or rather the circumstances which bring it about is as much a mystery as ever. You cannot trifle with Influenza. It unaermines the Nrreous System to a greater extent than almost any other disease, and it is Pneumonia that kills, and Pneumonia strikes the man who imagines he had only a mild form of Influenza, and can go about the street just as usual. It can hardly be doubted that the prevalence of Chest and Lung Com- plaints must be ascribed to the baneful infleenee of In- fluenza. whose after effects so frequently take this form. It was a bad day for this Country when this malignant scourge first visited our shores. Year after year it has never since failed to revive at its due time, and to extort its tribute of human life. Having observed its ravages and its dreadful effects upon the coustitutioe on the occasion ot its former visits, we cannot but regard its recurrence with much fear, as a great many have not yet, if they ever wilt, regain their former health. As a Preventative, we know of nothing equal to Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters. A fee; strong doses taken ins time have often Droved effectual in vsardine off attacks of OW Malady, and always succeel in mitigating thei severity when a patient is under their influence. Do you suffer from Chills, alternating with Sudden Flushes, Severe Headache, accompanied by difficulty of breath- ing. and symptoms of Catarrh, Pains in the Chest under and between the Shoulders, and a stiffness and soreness of the Muscles, Loss of Appetite and Nervousness. If you suffer from any of these symptoms, know that they are the forerunners of Influenza, and it behoves you to esort at once to a course of Gwilvm Evans' Quinine Bit- ters. By common consent Patients every whete admit that they feel more depressed and miserable after an at- tack of Influenza than while under its influence, and more than they feel after an attack of any other illness. The best way to banish these miserable feelines is to take Gwilem Evans' Quinine Bitters, The Veeetable Tonic. We can strongly and confidently recommend this Preparation, as it has treated severe Ca9"sl of Influenza, fleavy Colds, Extreme Weakness and Lan- gout, with greater success than any other known Remedy. We may also add that as a remedy for Indiges- tion. Sleeplessness, Lew Sphets, Nervousness, and Loss of ApPetite. Crwi:ym Evans' Qeinine Bitters eta.nde un- equalled. It is sold in bottles 2s 93 and 4s 6d., be all Chemists, and Patent Medicine Vendors, or direct car- riage free, I r the above peices, by tele 71 "Fonrietors : Qeinine Bit ers Manufacturing Company, bisaited, Lianelly, South Wales. Avoid Imitations. See the name " Gwilym Evans" on Label Stamp, and Bottle.</p>
