        <p>The Cup Sub-Committee mat in Manchester on Friday night, and selected the following officials for the first round of the Cup, to be played ell Saturday next on the grounds of the first-named clubs ; klck-off 3 30:— Dewsbury • Wigan, referee B Ashton (Oldham), touch judges If W Depledge (Huddersfield) and (1 Bruce (Heck- mon twike); Norrnanton • Leeds, referee A Brown (Brig- house), touch judges F Morrell (Bradford) and C Ackroyd (Bramley); Outwood Church • Widnes. referee S WilLiams (Salfori), touch judges W Castle (Castle- ford) and H Hartley (Wand); Huddersfield v Idle. refeeee W Beirstow (riunslat), touch judges S Ramadan (Brighouse) and J FL Hartley (Halifax); tetock- port • Hunslet, referee J Oakland (Outwood Church), touch judges J A Squires (Broughton Rangers) and ti Street (Altrincharn) , Ossett v. Elland, referee F T Rowlands (Brad- ford), touch judges G Fowler (Leeds) and 3 Henry (Holteck); Castleford • Batley, referee F Renton (Hunslet). touch jurius 14 Bell (Hull) anti A Fieldhouse (Holbeck) ; Altrinchem • Pontefract, referee J Ragland (Huddersfield), touch judges R Abbey (Stock eon) and J el'Go wan (B:coughton Rangers) ; Manninghana • Oldham, referee J H Smith (Widnes). to eh judges W Ernmott (Leeds) and G Greenwood (Leeds Parish Church) ; Holbeck •. Whitehaven Town, Whitehaven Town seratcued ; Morecainbe • Whitehiecn Recreation. referee J Kidd (Millorn), touch judges W 51 Donald ,Uivers- , ton) aad W IL Gelder (Daiton) ; Salford v York, referee J Sectinan (Liversedge), touch judees IL Beswiett (swinton) and P Ingle.= (Oldham); Broughton Rangers • Lane .ster, referee R H Moore (Oldham), touch judges W I Clege (Stockport) and A Bortlawick (it. Helens) ; Halifax • Fee herstone, referee T If Marshall (Brad- ford); touch judeee J H Barker (Liversedge) 'and S Waddington (Bramley); Winclhill • Rochdale Hornets referee F Kennedy (Broughton Range .8), touch judges H G Somers (Bradford) and B Woodhead (Hilend) ; Liversedge • Leigh, referee J Bruckshaw (Stocknort;, touch judges H Whiteley (Wakefield Trinity)end S Mortimer (Dewebury);Leeds. Parish Church • Seaton referee J Underwood (Wigeu),touch judges Holdsworth (Halifax) and W Raynor (Batley) ; llnneorn v Birstall, referee A Brooke (Brighouse Hangers), touch judges A Wailworki(Leigh) and W Atkinson (Wigan) ; Tyldesley • Brooktand Rovers, referee J E Newton (Altrincham), touch judges R S Davie ,(Brough! on Rangers)and B Telford(Salford); Hull • Wath Brow.referee H H Nuttall (Rochdale Helmets), touch judges T P Wilkinson (Leeds) and H Edmondson (Bradford) ; Alverthorpe • Workington. referee 11, Holmes (Rochdale Hornets). touch judges T H Hughes (Brighouse) and J F Shires (Bestmoor) : Birkenhead Wanderers • Wer- netb, referee P W Hancock (Runcorn), touch judges A Critchlay (Widnes) and J Barnes (Warrington) ; Bothwell • Bramley, Bothwell defunct; Swinton • Eastmeor. referee W Robinson (Manninghant),touch judges T L Brimelow (Salford) and T Melledew (Rochdale Hornets) ; Hull Kingston Rovers • Millom. referee W M'Cutcheon (Oldham), touch judges J Pickles (Leeds) and W Jackson (Leeds Parish Cuurch) Wakefield Trinity • Hebden Bridge, referee J W Porter (Hull), touch judges B Green (£llland) and J W Scholes (Dewsbury) ; rite Helene • Warrington, referee J Priestley (Broughton Rangers), touch judges W H Taylor (Stockport) and A, G Paul (Svriutoa) ; Kendal Hor- nets • Maryport, referee J Handyside (Morecanabe), touch judges J Gardner (Lancaster) and W B Banjemin (Askhatn); Barrow • Bradford. referee W Eddison ( Whack), touch judges W Teesdale (Mi torn) and J Roberts (Fleetwood); Goole • Reekmondwike, referee W Care (Hunslet). touch judges F Morton (Castleforcl) and L Whitehead ('full); Brig- house Ilaneers • Todmorden, referee F W Lowrie (Batley), touch judges J Gaunt (Bramley) and P F Farrar (Halifax) ; Radcliffe • Whitworth, referee J Graham (St;. Helens), touch judges .r Smith (Rochd its Hornets) and F Burnett (Werneth).</p>
