      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-03-16_WidnesExaminer_art0104" n="art0104">
        <head>ST. HELENS FOOTBALL CLUBS AND THE WIGAN CUP.</head>
        <p>ST. HELENS FOOTBALL CLUBS AND THE WIGAN CUP.</p>
        <p>A Protest by Parr</p>
        <p>Owing to the reported disbandmout of the Wigan County Footb-ill Clu'o, who bad won their way into the semi-final round for the Wigan Charity Cup, it 13 stated that the committee intend to give St. Helens Recreation and Warriinton another chance for the cup. These clubs had been knocked out by Wigan, and it is sugges- ted that tbe:y- should play another match to decide which should play Prescot in the semi-final. This decision will no doubt be welcomed by the Recreation and War- rington. At the conclusion of the serni-final at St. Flolens, OR Saturday, between Haydock and Parr, two local clubs, it was stated that the Parr officials would protest against Haydock. The officials state that before the match they knew that some of the Haydock players were not eligible for the competition. Then they recy,ard two or thrre of the paid crei by Haydock a.s exleedingly doubtful that they cannot ellJcv the result to stand without pro- test.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-03-16_WidnesExaminer_art0105" n="art0105">
