        <p>Mr. ?Senor, Dear Sir,—Allow me to tender my sincere thanks to you for the great benefit I received whilst under your treatment with my eyes. I was recommended to you by a little boy at the station, I came, and after three (3) visits was soon able to see again. You are at liberty to do with this as you think propor. Yours truly, THOMAS FR ANGLETON. 1. Howley-lane, Warrington.</p>
        <p>Sir,—l write to thank you for the good you have done or my eyes alter so abort a treatment (3 weeks.) The change hr truly remarkable. With pleasure I shall commend you treatment ang answer any inquiry. Again thanking you. I remain, yours sincerely, BEN HALL.</p>
